{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:84a2ff2e0a330fd0","name":"C-Wing Ugly Fighter","source":{"id":"source:reference-84a2ff2e0a330fd0","title":"C-Wing Ugly Fighter","revision":19619,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:17:56Z","sha256":"34bebd2836da8a88083906c0ef07546d80b3c2fc60bccac359727bbcfedc002a","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19619","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=C-Wing%20Ugly%20Fighter&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-84a2ff2e0a330fd0","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The C-Wing, also known as the Corellian/B-Wing Ugly, is a typical example of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," built from pieces found floating about after a major ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," battle. Though the exact configurations of C-Wings vary, they are essentially a YT-series light freighter cockpit bolted on to a B-Wing's main fuselage.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["These Uglies originally came about because ",{"tag":"a","children":["The New Republic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_New_Republic","referenceId":"reference:e6046dbb57e5abb0"}," determined that if a B-Wing's battle damage included its complex gyrating cockpit section, it was cheaper to build a new ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," than to repair the complicated mechanism. Thus, many ",{"tag":"a","children":["B-Wings"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/B-Wings"}," with that damage were left behind at battle sites. The C-Wing design gets around this problem by taking out the rotating component entirely, and turning the ",{"tag":"a","children":["B-Wing"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/B-Wing"}," fuselage sidewise in normal flight.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The big freighter cockpit gives the fighter room for a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Pilot"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Pilot","referenceId":"reference:4aff6d0e54fff36e"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"},", as well as two passengers. Though passenger seats normally sit empty, the C-Wing could be used as a short range armed shuttle. The spacious accommodations (by ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"}," standards) also allow a C-Wing to go on longer-range missions than normal, in relative comfort. In fact, if a C-Wing were to sacrifice firepower for a sensor suite, it might make a fair scout fighter.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Normal)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["C-Wing Ugly Fighter Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Gargantuan (",{"tag":"a","children":["Unreliable"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unreliable"},") ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +1; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 13 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 12), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 23; +7 Armor\n"]},{"tag":"p","ch